<!--
Rendered into the Epic description as markdown. Keep every heading, in this
order: a reader scanning a board relies on the same sections being in the same
places. Delete this comment when rendering.

A section with nothing to say gets an explicit "None known" or "Not yet
decided" -- never an empty heading, which reads as an oversight rather than a
decision, and never a deleted heading, which hides that the question was asked.
-->

## Outcome

<What is true after this epic ships that is not true now. One paragraph, in
terms of the people affected rather than the components changed.>

## Problem

<What is wrong today, and what it costs. Evidence rather than assertion where
evidence exists.>

## Scope

<What is in. Bullet the workstreams, not the tickets -- the stories under this
epic are where tickets live.>

## Out of scope

<What a reasonable reader would assume is included and is not. This section
prevents more rework than any other.>

## Success criteria

<How anyone can tell this worked, stated so that the answer is yes or no.
Include the measure and where it is read from.>

## Dependencies

<Teams, systems, or decisions this epic waits on. Name the owner of each, or
say that it is unowned -- an unowned dependency is a risk, not a blank.>

## Technical notes

<Constraints, chosen approach, and anything already ruled out with the reason.>

## Links

<Specs, designs, prior discussion. Links only, never copied content: copied
content goes stale where it sits, and nobody knows which copy is current.>
